{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"codex_apps","tool":"github.get_pr_info","arguments":{"repository_full_name":"stranske/Workflows","pr_number":3836},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Action completed."}],"structured_content":{"url":"https://github.com/stranske/Workflows/pull/3836","number":3836,"state":"open","merged":false,"mergeable":true,"draft":false,"body":"Closes #3835.\n\nThe verifier discarded mandatory artifact delivery, PR/inline review-comment destinations, and validation-output checklist evidence, allowing a model PASS despite missing named evidence. This change retains those destinations through the existing polarity/product/literal and destination-OR grammar, with the source and consumer template kept byte-identical.\n\n## Tasks\n\n- [x] Extend `scripts/langchain/pr_verifier.py::_required_evidence_channels` shared artifact operation/destination grammar to recognize active evidence delivery using `as an artifact`.\n- [x] Extend `scripts/langchain/pr_verifier.py::_required_evidence_channels` shared review destination vocabulary for PR review comments and inline review comments.\n- [x] Extend `scripts/langchain/pr_verifier.py::_required_evidence_channels` checklist noun handling using existing common-proof/polarity vocabulary so Validation output/results retain the named comment destination.\n- [x] Add direct RED/GREEN cases to `tests/scripts/test_pr_verifier_delivery_destinations.py` for the three original examples and bounded positive/negative/optional/product/literal controls.\n- [x] Add destination-specific coverage-floor regressions to `tests/scripts/test_pr_verifier_prompt_coverage.py` with body present but comments absent/unavailable, and body present but artifacts absent/unavailable.\n- [x] Synchronize `templates/consumer-repo/scripts/langchain/pr_verifier.py` with the source fix.\n- [x] Update the existing verifier entry in `.github/sync-manifest.yml` and the boundary contract in `docs/ops/CONSUMER_REPO_MAINTENANCE.md`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `python -m pytest tests/scripts/test_pr_verifier_delivery_destinations.py tests/scripts/test_pr_verifier_prompt_coverage.py -q` passes on the fixed bytes; deliberate restoration of each original grammar defect makes its named regression fail, followed by byte-identical restoration and GREEN.\n- [x] `Attach evidence as an artifact` and `Upload the coverage report as an artifact` require artifacts, and missing/unavailable artifacts block a model PASS even with a present PR body.\n- [x] `Evidence must be posted in a PR review comment` and the inline-review-comment variant require comments; absent/unavailable comments cannot be masked by a present PR body.\n- [x] `- [x] Validation output in a PR comment` requires comments; negative, optional, quoted-literal and product-capability controls remain nongating unless a separate mandatory delivery exists.\n- [x] Source and `templates/consumer-repo/scripts/langchain/pr_verifier.py` are byte-identical for the changed verifier, with manifest/docs coverage and retained RED/GREEN commands/results in the ready implementation PR.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Complete two-module gate: `python -m pytest tests/scripts/test_pr_verifier_delivery_destinations.py tests/scripts/test_pr_verifier_prompt_coverage.py -q -o addopts= -n 4`: **92,822 passed**, zero failures/errors/skips.\n- Original focused reproduction: **14 failed, 14 passed**; fixed focused gate: **28 passed**.\n- Three independent production-rule reversals: each gives **3 failures**, followed by exact byte restoration and **3 passes** on the same direct/floor nodes. Both source copies restore to SHA256 `a743cbfed0bdd653a2a33ee3061650b75175d84ded1031604908343c12fc9c53`.\n- Black, Ruff, diff check, source/template comparison and template-completeness validation passed. Manifest/docs gate: **2 passed, 1 existing skip**.\n- `docs/evidence/issue-3835-evidence-destinations/` retains the replay, exact commands/process receipts, full raw logs/JUnit and SHA256 manifest; all 28 archive-member hashes and five current input hashes verified.\n\nThis proves the bounded local grammar and coverage-floor contract. Native-provider acceptance, #3820/#3831 capture partitioning and downstream promotion/reconciliation remain separate work. The initial serial run was intentionally interrupted and then replaced by the complete four-worker run; its partial logs are retained without a full-gate claim.\n\n<!-- pr-preamble:start -->\n<!-- meta:issue:3835 -->\n> **Source:** Issue #3835\n\nCloses #3835\n\n<!-- pr-preamble:end -->\n\n<!-- auto-status-summary:start -->\n## Automated Status Summary\n#### Scope\nCurrent delivered Workflows source `49286cc28411f1efb5545866ed0f278e6c680fdb`, `scripts/langchain/pr_verifier.py` in `_required_evidence_channels` (consumer lines 3886/4037), still loses three mandatory evidence destinations. Actual trip-planner #1885 head `b28e40427fe68fb9848d0a988a9149463e10058c` findings https://github.com/stranske/trip-planner/pull/1885#discussion_r4242755333 and https://github.com/stranske/trip-planner/pull/1885#discussion_r4242755339 reproduce: `Attach evidence as an artifact` returns no channel; `Evidence must be posted in a PR review comment` returns overall instead of comments. Independently reproduced `- [ ] Validation output in a PR comment` also returns no channel. This is a current deterministic completeness defect, not optional stylistic coverage. Required evidence can be missing while a model PASS survives the floor.\n\n<!-- Updated WORKFLOW_OUTPUTS.md context:start -->\n## Context for Agent\n\n### Related Issues/PRs\n- [stranske/trip-planner#1885](https://github.com/stranske/trip-planner/issues/1885)\n- [stranske/Workflows#3836](https://github.com/stranske/Workflows/issues/3836)\n- [#1885](https://github.com/stranske/Workflows/issues/1885)\n- [#3820](https://github.com/stranske/Workflows/issues/3820)\n- [#3831](https://github.com/stranske/Workflows/issues/3831)\n<!-- Updated WORKFLOW_OUTPUTS.md context:end -->\n\n#### Tasks\n- [x] Extend `scripts/langchain/pr_verifier.py::_required_evidence_channels` shared artifact operation/destination grammar to recognize active evidence delivery using `as an artifact`.\n- [x] Extend `scripts/langchain/pr_verifier.py::_required_evidence_channels` shared review destination vocabulary for PR review comments and inline review comments.\n- [x] Extend `scripts/langchain/pr_verifier.py::_required_evidence_channels` checklist noun handling using existing common-proof/polarity vocabulary so Validation output/results retain the named comment destination.\n- [x] Add direct RED/GREEN cases to `tests/scripts/test_pr_verifier_delivery_destinations.py` for the three original examples and bounded positive/negative/optional/product/literal controls.\n- [x] Add destination-specific coverage-floor regressions to `tests/scripts/test_pr_verifier_prompt_coverage.py` with body present but comments absent/unavailable, and body present but artifacts absent/unavailable.\n- [x] Synchronize `templates/consumer-repo/scripts/langchain/pr_verifier.py` with the source fix.\n- [x] Update the existing verifier entry in `.github/sync-manifest.yml` and the boundary contract in `docs/ops/CONSUMER_REPO_MAINTENANCE.md`.\n\n#### Acceptance criteria\n- [x] `python -m pytest tests/scripts/test_pr_verifier_delivery_destinations.py tests/scripts/test_pr_verifier_prompt_coverage.py -q` passes on the fixed bytes; deliberate restoration of each original grammar defect makes its named regression fail, followed by byte-identical restoration and GREEN.\n- [x] `Attach evidence as an artifact` and `Upload the coverage report as an artifact` require artifacts, and missing/unavailable artifacts block a model PASS even with a present PR body.\n- [x] `Evidence must be posted in a PR review comment` and the inline-review-comment variant require comments; absent/unavailable comments cannot be masked by a present PR body.\n- [x] `- [ ] Validation output in a PR comment` requires comments; negative, optional, quoted-literal and product-capability controls remain nongating unless a separate mandatory delivery exists.\n- [x] Source and `templates/consumer-repo/scripts/langchain/pr_verifier.py` are byte-identical for the changed verifier, with manifest/docs coverage and retained RED/GREEN commands/results in the ready implementation PR.\n\n<!-- auto-status-summary:end -->","title":"fix(verifier): retain artifact and review-comment evidence destinations","base":"main","base_sha":"6020028dec510c931364fb69f63dc2a2aa297689","head":"codex/issue-3835","head_sha":"430d1b457c3c068a951f76962a61c0b5ce97a93b","head_repo_id":1117447156,"head_repo_full_name":"stranske/Workflows","merge_commit_sha":"9999c8e495fe54f3327dafa93ecf4a6e1925e222","user":{"login":"stranske","name":"stranske","email":null,"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23046322?v=4","id":23046322},"requested_reviewers":null,"requested_team_reviewers":null,"diff":null,"comments":null,"created_at":"2026-10-11T19:24:38Z","updated_at":"2026-10-11T20:05:08Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"commits":3,"changed_files":12,"additions":575,"deletions":3,"display_url":"https://github.com/stranske/Workflows/pull/3836","display_title":"fix(verifier): retain artifact and review-comment evidence destinations"}},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
