>\n</dl>\n</details>\n<hr>\n\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>📝 Summary</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Summary by CodeRabbit</h2>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><strong>New Features</strong>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Evidence requirements now recognize named workflow artifacts and PR review comments, including inline comments. Checklist items also accept common test, validation, build, and execution proof.</li>\n<li>Alternative destinations joined by “or” are handled as separate evidence options, while quoted text remains literal.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Bug Fixes</strong>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>A PR body no longer satisfies a requirement for comments or artifacts when that evidence is missing or unavailable.</li>\n<li>Evidence requirements remain enforced regardless of capacity, and receipt I/O warnings do not affect capacity outcomes.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Documentation</strong>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Updated guidance clarifies evidence destinations and checklist proof requirements.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>📝 Summary</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Walkthrough</h2>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The verifier now recognizes artifact and PR review-comment evidence destinations, including checklist proof nouns. Tests check required-channel detection and ensure missing or unavailable evidence cannot be replaced by PR-body evidence. The PR also adds mutation replay tooling and records local test results and hashes.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Changes</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Evidence destination handling</strong></p>\n<markdown-accessiblity-table><table role=\"table\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th align=\"left\">Layer / File(s)</th>\n<th align=\"left\">Summary</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"left\"><strong>Destination grammar and coverage floor</strong> <br> <code class=\"notranslate\">scripts/langchain/pr_verifier.py</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">templates/consumer-repo/scripts/langchain/pr_verifier.py</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">tests/scripts/test_pr_verifier_delivery_destinations.py</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">tests/scripts/test_pr_verifier_prompt_coverage.py</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">.github/sync-manifest.yml</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">docs/ops/CONSUMER_REPO_MAINTENANCE.md</code></td>\n<td align=\"left\">Both verifier copies normalize recognized PR review-comment phrases to <code class=\"notranslate\">PR comment</code>, recognize proof aliases in checklist requirements, and classify evidence delivered as workflow artifacts. Tests cover positive and non-gating cases, destination alternatives, and coverage-floor behavior when a required channel is absent or unavailable. The manifest description and maintenance guide document the expanded grammar and its boundaries.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"left\"><strong>Mutation replay</strong> <br> <code class=\"notranslate\">docs/evidence/issue-3835-evidence-destinations/replay.py</code></td>\n<td align=\"left\">The replay script creates three verifier mutations, checks expected test outcomes against mutated and restored sources, restores source files, and writes receipts and output hashes.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"left\"><strong>Validation records</strong> <br> <code class=\"notranslate\">docs/evidence/issue-3835-evidence-destinations/README.md</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">docs/evidence/issue-3835-evidence-destinations/manifest.json</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">docs/evidence/issue-3835-evidence-destinations/followup-validation.json</code></td>\n<td align=\"left\">The records report test commands and results, source and artifact hashes, replay outcomes, and the stated limits of local validation.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Priority:</strong> ➖ Normal</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Estimated code review effort:</strong> 3 (Moderate) | ~25 minutes</p>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Change:</strong> Bug 