om/f2c1aacb361ddd3a0e9f9cacdb84fab050de434017f6747bb916e31e29bdf03d/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f50322d79656c6c6f773f7374796c653d666c6174\"><img src=\"https://camo.githubusercontent.com/f2c1aacb361ddd3a0e9f9cacdb84fab050de434017f6747bb916e31e29bdf03d/68747470733a2f2f696d672e736869656c64732e696f2f62616467652f50322d79656c6c6f773f7374796c653d666c6174\" alt=\"P2 Badge\" data-canonical-src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"></a></sub></sub>  Honor negative governors for as-artifact clauses</strong></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">When acceptance text uses noun-form negation, such as <code class=\"notranslate\">No need to attach evidence as an artifact</code>, this new unconditional operation/object match makes <code class=\"notranslate\">_required_evidence_channels</code> return <code class=\"notranslate\">{\"artifacts\"}</code>; the parent implementation returned no required channel. Consequently, an absent artifact can now downgrade a model PASS to CONCERNS even though the criterion explicitly says the delivery is unnecessary. Route this match through the shared negative-governor handling or exclude <code class=\"notranslate\">no need</code>/<code class=\"notranslate\">no requirement</code> contexts.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.</p>"},{"url":"https://github.com/stranske/Workflows/pull/3836#pullrequestreview-5484629614","body":"\n### 💡 Codex Review\n\nHere are some automated review suggestions for this pull request.\n\n**Reviewed commit:** `85f990cfca`\n    \n\n<details> <summary>ℹ️ About Codex in GitHub</summary>\n<br/>\n\n[Your team has set up Codex to review pull requests in this repo](https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/settings/general). Reviews are triggered when you\n- Open a pull request for review\n- Mark a draft as ready\n- Comment \"@codex review\".\n\nIf Codex has suggestions, it will comment; otherwise it will react with 👍.\n\n\n\n\nCodex can also answer questions or update the PR